; Singularity VR mod - settings
;
; NOTE: there is deliberately no resolution setting here.
;
; Forcing the D3D9 backbuffer size does NOT raise UE3's render resolution. The
; engine allocates its scene render targets from its own configured resolution,
; so overriding the backbuffer only desynchronises the two - the engine keeps
; rendering at its old size into a larger buffer, and stereo switches itself off
; because the scene target no longer matches. Tried in run 14; it broke badly.
;
; To change the render resolution, use the game's own VIDEO OPTIONS menu. That
; makes the engine allocate its scene targets at the new size, which is what
; actually raises the per-eye pixel density.
;
; Why you'd want to: with true stereo each eye gets half the width, so at
; 2560x1440 an eye sees only 1280x1440 - roughly 14 pixels per degree at full
; FOV, against the headset's ~25. That undersampling is what makes textures
; shimmer. Raising the game's resolution is the fix; narrowing the FOV
; (PAGE DOWN) is only a workaround that trades field of view for sharpness.
;
; Expect the frame rate to fall as resolution rises - the frame copy is still a
; CPU round-trip. That is the next thing to fix (D3D9Ex zero-copy).

[Render]
